# ==============================================================================
# File: .gitattributes
#
# Purpose:
#   Fixes the form every tracked file takes in the working tree and in a diff.
#   Two classes of defect are addressed, and both are of the kind this project
#   exists to make visible rather than to tolerate: a line ending that changes
#   between one contributor's checkout and another's, and a file whose contents
#   a textual diff would corrupt or merely obscure.
#
# Contents:
#   1. Line endings.
#   2. Files that are not text.
#   3. Diff and language attributes.
#
# References:
#   - gitattributes(5): the `text`, `eol`, `binary`, `diff` and `export-ignore`
#     attributes, and the `linguist-*` attributes GitHub reads.
#   - docs/project/CODING-STANDARDS.md: indentation is four spaces
#     and tabulation characters appear only where GNU Make requires them.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF,
# on every platform. `eol=lf` is stated rather than left to core.autocrlf
# because the failure it prevents is silent and remote: this repository is
# presently worked upon from WSL, where a checkout carrying CRLF produces an
# assembler that reports an error at a line that looks correct, a shell script
# that fails with an unprintable character in the message, and a linker script
# whose fault is visible to nobody reading it.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*               text=auto eol=lf

*.c             text eol=lf
*.h             text eol=lf
*.asm           text eol=lf
*.s             text eol=lf
*.S             text eol=lf
*.ld            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Files that are not text.
#
# These are marked so that git neither converts their line endings nor attempts
# a textual merge upon them. A bootable image or a font whose bytes a merge had
# rewritten would fail at the machine rather than at the tool.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.iso           binary
*.img           binary
*.bin           binary
*.elf           binary
*.o             binary
*.a             binary
*.psf           binary
*.fd            binary
*.vdi           binary
*.qcow2         binary
*.png           binary

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Diff and language attributes.
#
# `diff=cpp` gives the hunk headers of a C diff the enclosing function's name,
# which is the difference between reading a patch and locating it first.
#
# The linguist attributes govern the language summary GitHub presents. The
# documentation of this project is a large part of it by volume and is meant to
# be; counted as source it would report the repository as chiefly prose, and
# `linguist-documentation` keeps it out of the count without hiding it from a
# search. The licence texts are nobody's work here and are marked vendored.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.c             diff=cpp
*.h             diff=cpp

*.md            linguist-documentation
docs/**         linguist-documentation
LICENSES/**     linguist-vendored
.github/**      linguist-vendored
